// The RSA-OAEP negative-composition probe world: the minimal consumer of
// `rsa-oaep-decrypt`, which the in-guest provider deliberately does not
// export (class D — see rust/guest-provider/README.md). The class-D gate
// (`just conformance::class-d`) builds a dummy component of this world and
// asserts it does NOT compose with the provider.
//
// The signing guest cannot prove this: its composition already fails on
// `ecdsa-sign`, so a provider that wrongly started exporting the OAEP
// decryption mints would still fail that composition for an unrelated
// reason. This world imports nothing the provider withholds except
// `rsa-oaep-decrypt` itself, so its composition failure can only come
// from the OAEP kind-export mechanics: the provider exports the generic
// `public-encryption` interface, so `wac plug` rebinds its resources to
// the provider's exports and orphans the `rsa-oaep-decrypt` import that
// still names the imported ones.
//
// The `lann:webcrypto` package lives once at the repository root `wit/`,
// pulled in through the `deps/lann-webcrypto` symlink.
package conformance:class-d-oaep-probe;

world oaep-probe {
    @unstable(feature = rsa-oaep-decrypt)
    import lann:webcrypto/rsa-oaep-decrypt@0.1.0;
}
